      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 Cardiological Society of India. Published by Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Anomalous origin of right coronary artery (RCA) from left sinus is a rare clinical entity. Percutaneous coronary intervention of such an anomalous RCA, which is chronically occluded, is difficult and is rarely described. We describe such an intervention in a patient, who had a chronic total occlusion of anomalous RCA and discuss the technical issues associated with such interventions."
      },
